title: Activity log loses entries under concurrency -- read-modify-write with no CAS
updated: 2026-08-13T02:21:53Z
---

Found in a bug hunt; reproduced by the finder and independently
re-reproduced by me, five out of five rounds.

ActivityLog.pm:206-228 reads the whole log ref, appends one line, and writes
it back with the unguarded, last-writer-wins write_ref:

    my $existing = $self->git->read_ref($ref);
    my $new = $existing ? "$existing\n$line" : $line;
    return try { $self->git->write_ref($ref, $new) } ...

Two commands that read the same content both write their own single-line
append; the loser's entry disappears. The log ref is keyed by Git identity
and every agent in one clone shares user.email, so this is the NORMAL path
on the multi-agent boards karr is built for, not an exotic race.

allocate_next_id_ref and save_task_cas got compare-and-swap for exactly this
reason (#44, #86). The log did not.

My reproduction -- 24 parallel `karr create` in one repo, five rounds:

    Runde 1: Task-Refs=24  Log-Eintraege=20  <<< VERLUST
    Runde 2: Task-Refs=24  Log-Eintraege=20  <<< VERLUST
    Runde 3: Task-Refs=24  Log-Eintraege=20  <<< VERLUST
    Runde 4: Task-Refs=24  Log-Eintraege=20  <<< VERLUST
    Runde 5: Task-Refs=24  Log-Eintraege=20  <<< VERLUST

(A 16-way run happened to come out clean once, so a regression test needs
enough parallelism to be reliable -- 24 was deterministic here.)

Cost: the audit trail under-reports, permanently and silently. karr log,
karr context (last_entry) and any handoff reconstruction see a board where
work happened that nobody did. The tasks themselves are fine -- only the log
loses entries.
